## Owner rulings applied (Karl, 2026-06-07)

**R1 — Doc 05 family controls (CC-P2-016 = Reading A).** Doc 02C V4 is superseded for mastery/domain/KPI/projection formulas, constants, difficulty scale, and RPC names. Consequence: the deployed mastery/scoring stack — which coherently implements the Doc 02C V4 generation end-to-end (CC2-008 corroboration) — is classified wrong-generation. Dispositions across zone MA and EX-02 are BUILD (implement the locked Doc 05/04B generation), not parameter-tuning. Corpus action: SP-01.

**R2 — Guardian grace-period carve-out (CC-P2-007 reconciliation = option b).** Coding-standards §6.2 is to be amended so guardian visibility persists through the Doc 01-defined entitlement grace window (SP-02). The entitlement-omission half of CC-P2-007 is therefore a spec revision, not a code defect. The function defect that remains: `is_guardian_of` checks only `profiles.guardian_profile_id` linkage — no link-active/revoked-status check, no grace-window bound — so a revoked link whose denormalized pointer is stale still grants access (GAP-ID-01).

## Severity scheme (final, no longer provisional)

CRITICAL = data-boundary exposure, minors-data/privacy exposure, or core-IP/correctness failure that must close before any launch consideration. HIGH = invariant violation or canonical-contract miss with material product/compliance effect. MEDIUM = spec violation with bounded blast radius or strong mitigation. LOW = hygiene/debt.

Where auditors disagreed, the registry severity is the arbitrated one and the entry notes the arbitration (e.g., CX2-E-002/003/004 CRITICAL → consolidated under the single wrong-generation CRITICAL at GAP-MA-01, sub-components HIGH/MEDIUM).

## Status legend

- **OPEN** — confirmed gap, evidence complete, ready for closure planning
- **VERIFY(VP-nn)** — claim from one auditor lacking evidence or contradicted by the other; final disposition pending the Verification Pass (`03-verification-pass/verification-pass-prompt.md`)
- **SPEC-REVISION** — corpus change item produced by a ruling or ambiguity (docs/Spec edits happen through the normal lock-cycle process, never by auditors)
- **CONFORMANT** — verified correct; recorded so "verified" is distinguishable from "unexamined"

## Disposition vocabulary

BUILD (greenfield implementation of locked spec) | FIX-DB (policy/grant/schema/function correction) | FIX-CODE (app-layer correction) | RETIRE (remove superseded object after replacement lands) | CLEANUP (legacy/hygiene removal) | PROCESS (pipeline/provenance work) | SPEC-REVISION.

## Standing rules

- The registry is the single source of truth for the closure plan. The COO-hat closure plan is derived FROM this registry after the Verification Pass returns; phasing is not pre-designed.
- Every closure PR cites the GAP ID(s) it closes and updates the registry status in the same PR.
- `docs/Spec/` remains read-only; SP items route through the spec lock-cycle.
- Severities here are final unless the Verification Pass overturns a VERIFY entry's factual basis.

## V1.1 addendum (2026-06-07)

Verification Pass complete: dual-agent (Claude Code + Codex, independent), corroborating verdicts on all seven items. All VERIFY entries finalized; constants dump analyzed (owner-confirmed: `mastery_constants` + `kpi_constants` are the only constants tables; all Doc 05/04B-generation constants are new implementations). Registry V1.1 (`gap-registry.md`) is self-contained — raw auditor reports are NOT committed to the repo; decisive evidence is inline. Execution view: `closure-plan.md` (WS-0..WS-7 + WS-S), derived from the registry, 66/66 gaps mapped.
